From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winsta: Implement WinStationEnumerateW and
 WinStationBroadcastSystemMessage.

The sessions are the numbered directories of \Sessions: session 0, the services', and the one on the
screen.  WinStationBroadcastSystemMessage is BroadcastSystemMessage to the desktops of another
session, or of all of them, which is how a service in session 0 tells the programs of the user's
session about a device: a BroadcastSystemMessage of its own reaches the desktops of session 0 only.

winsta.h moves to include, for the modules that broadcast.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

